diff --git a/source/diagnosticreport/diagnosticreport-notes.xml b/source/diagnosticreport/diagnosticreport-notes.xml
index 5caf9e221e..58e93bf6eb 100644
--- a/source/diagnosticreport/diagnosticreport-notes.xml
+++ b/source/diagnosticreport/diagnosticreport-notes.xml
@@ -9,12 +9,12 @@ Notes:
 <h3>Clinically Relevant Time</h3>
 	<p>
 The best practice is to always include an <a href="diagnosticreport-definitions.html#DiagnosticReport.effective_x_">effective[x]</a> element.
-If specimens were taken, often the clinically relevant time of the report can be derived from the specimen collection times.
-However, detailed specimen information is not always available nor is the clinically relevant time always exactly the specimen collection time (e.g. complex timed tests). Note that <a href="http://www.hl7.org/implement/standards/product_brief.cfm?product_id=185">HL7 V2</a> messages often carry a diagnostically relevant time without carrying any specimen information.
+If specimens were taken, often the clinically relevant time of the report can be derived from the specimen collection times. However, detailed specimen information is not always available nor is the clinically relevant time always exactly the specimen collection time (e.g. complex timed tests). 
+Note that <a href="http://www.hl7.org/implement/standards/product_brief.cfm?product_id=185">HL7 V2</a> messages often carry a diagnostically relevant time without carrying any specimen information.
 </p>
 <h3>Associated Observations</h3>
 <blockquote class="ballot-note">
-<p><b>Note to Balloters:</b> The following guidance on DiagnosticReport and Observation grouping patterns has been revised for R6. Balloters are asked to review whether the two patterns, related search guidance, and use of organizer Observations are clear and implementable across all domains. In particular, feedback is requested from laboratory implementers on whether terms such as "panel" and the laboratory result handling guidance are clear and do not hinder current or planned implementations, and from non-laboratory implementers on whether the guidance is too laboratory-centric or needs broader wording. Specific examples and additional content would be welcomed. Balloters are also asked to review this text for consistency with the Diagnostics Module and Observation grouping guidance.</p>
+<p><b>Note to Balloters:</b> The following guidance on DiagnosticReport and Observation grouping patterns has been revised for R6. Balloters are asked to review whether the two patterns, related search guidance, and use of organizer Observations are clear and implementable across all domains. In particular, feedback is requested from laboratory implementers on whether terms such as "panel" and the laboratory result handling guidance are clear and do not hinder current or planned implementations, and from non-laboratory implementers on whether the guidance is too laboratory-centric or needs broader wording. Specific examples and additional content would be welcomed. Balloters are also asked to review this text for consistency with the Diagnostics Module and Observation grouping guidance.</p>
 </blockquote>
